title: "StateShift: Tracking State-Dependent Reasoning Recovery Across Post-Training"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
repository-code: "https://github.com/shamddd/stateshift"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: "StateShift investigates whether post-training reasoning models possess latent, recoverable reasoning trajectories when prompted to revisit intermediate mathematical states. Combining historical checkpoint analysis on DeepScaleR-7B (29,056 rollouts) and a pre-registered physical GPU trial on Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct (400 generations on NVIDIA RTX 4090), this repository provides end-to-end reproducibility code, exact discrete statistical power engines, and complete generation ledgers."
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - reasoning-recovery
  - reinforcement-learning
  - post-training
  - mathematical-reasoning
  - mcnemar-test
  - discrete-power
